AccountV3Execution
├── when the first UserOperation creates the account
│   ├── it transfers counterfactually funded native assets with real EntryPoint fees
│   ├── it binds the canonical call array and security version
│   └── completeCreation ends initialization; consumer needs no later activation
├── given an active account
│   ├── when CALL batches succeed
│   │   ├── it transfers native assets and ERC20 through arbitrary calldata
│   │   └── it supports 1 to 32 calls and rejects 0 or 33
│   ├── when a target fails
│   │   └── all asset effects roll back; EntryPoint nonce and gas remain consumed
│   ├── when using a direct signed relay
│   │   ├── no bundler, paymaster or GatoPago service is required
│   │   ├── separate nonce, mode, validity and signatures prevent replay/substitution
│   │   └── failed batches roll back direct nonce; retry is atomic
│   ├── when callbacks attempt nested execution or security mutations
│   │   └── reentrancy and the cross-domain executing flag block them
│   └── when another account changes security after batch validation
│       └── execution rechecks current version before any asset call
└── when sender, plan, calldata, domain or authorization is wrong
    └── reject without transferring assets
